                <pb facs="0593" n="489" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg489"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.00 Revolutions/197: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-09-13T17:00:00-04:00">September 13,
                            1932—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:21 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>205. Dávila resigned and delivered the power to his Minister of the Interior,
                    General Blanche, who was provisional Vice President and who declares that he
                    will carry out the Socialist idea. It is apparently a victory for Merino.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
